WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.092
Simulation is one of the most useful applications of NumPy.

00:00:04.092 --> 00:00:11.322
Instead of calculating a probability only with a formula, we can generate thousands of random outcomes and estimate the

00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:13.752
rate from the simulated results.

00:00:14.202 --> 00:00:22.984
For example, imagine repeatedly simulating whether an event occurs and then calculating the proportion of successful

00:00:22.984 --> 00:00:28.404
outcomes. With enough trials, the estimated rate should become reasonably stable.

00:00:28.404 --> 00:00:34.794
This same idea appears in risk analysis, Monte Carlo methods, forecasting, and statistical experiments.

00:00:34.794 --> 00:00:44.504
The key advantage of NumPy is that thousands or even millions of simulated values can be generated and summarized

00:00:44.504 --> 00:00:45.282
efficiently.
